and then our seats up the front and so we could&nbsp;
move back and forth through the vehicle through&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:37.520 --> 01:37:45.120
it. And so we sat there, my uncle did cocaine and&nbsp;
then he gave me more drugs. It was war on drugs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:45.120 --> 01:37:50.960
You know that when Kathy O'Brien talks about that&nbsp;
war on drugs, she ain't kidding because yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:50.960 --> 01:37:59.440
you are so hyped up on drugs. And then we went&nbsp;
from there from the airport loading up our gear&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:59.440 --> 01:38:05.840
to a warehouse. And at that warehouse, um there&nbsp;
was a warehouse there by the ocean somewhere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:05.840 --> 01:38:11.440
And that warehouse was scheduled for demolition.&nbsp;
And so we went and we went in this warehouse. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:11.440 --> 01:38:18.640
was pretty empty in there. There was a little&nbsp;
bit of stuff in there, but not much stuff.

01:38:18.640 --> 01:38:25.520
We went back in there and we parked the van and&nbsp;
then we um Oh, and I remember driving the van. My&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:25.520 --> 01:38:31.520
uncle made me drive it and I was like, Gail,&nbsp;
I'm so hyped up on drugs right now. How are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:31.520 --> 01:38:37.680
How am I supposed to drive this van? And he was&nbsp;
like, just drive. Let's go. You know? Yeah. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:37.680 --> 01:38:43.920
we're all hyped up on drugs, driving this van&nbsp;
around Japan. And we went to this warehouse&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:43.920 --> 01:38:52.080
and we parked in there and we ate lunch. Well, I&nbsp;
ate lunch. I can remember eating MREs. My uncle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:52.080 --> 01:38:57.200
he was going to go into the city to meet with&nbsp;
Cat and so he was going to go eat somewhere nice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:57.200 --> 01:39:06.000
but I ate um I ate MREs, I think two of them.&nbsp;
And yeah, just gross food. But then at that time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:06.000 --> 01:39:09.440
that's what that's what you ate, you know. I&nbsp;
didn't even think twice about it. I was like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:09.440 --> 01:39:16.000
"Yeah, give me my MREs." and we unloaded the van.&nbsp;
We had these black hard cases that all of our gear&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:16.000 --> 01:39:21.520
was stored in. I want to say they're a lot like&nbsp;
what's called, I believe, a Pelican case. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:21.520 --> 01:39:26.880
black hard cases and that's what we stored all&nbsp;
our gear in. And so we got all our gear out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:26.880 --> 01:39:32.320
van, went through it, put everything in there and&nbsp;
organized it how we wanted it, and then we took&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:32.320 --> 01:39:38.240
these hard cases that we didn't taking up all the&nbsp;
space in the van and we put them uh we hid them at&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:38.240 --> 01:39:43.680
the back of the warehouse. So this warehouse was&nbsp;
scheduled for demolition and so people weren't&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:43.680 --> 01:39:48.880
using it. I can remember the roof was falling in&nbsp;
in part of it. No one would ever think to think in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:48.880 --> 01:39:54.080
this dark corner of this place to find this kind&nbsp;
of stuff and they couldn't see us doing it either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:54.080 --> 01:40:00.560
Emma, that's another key is if there were planes,&nbsp;
helicopters, anything in the sky, you wouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:00.560 --> 01:40:06.640
see what we were doing or from the sides. We were&nbsp;
well hidden in there. And then I was put to sleep&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:06.640 --> 01:40:12.320
after I'd eaten my MREs because my uncle had to&nbsp;
go into the city and I don't know how long I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:12.320 --> 01:40:18.880
asleep for. The next thing I remember is waking&nbsp;
up in the van and just it was dark. I was like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:18.880 --> 01:40:26.960
where on earth am I? And I could hear my uncle&nbsp;
and he was talking to somebody over the calm&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:26.960 --> 01:40:33.520
system in the back of the van. I could hear it&nbsp;
and I started to wake up and I can remember at&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:33.520 --> 01:40:42.000
that time it was really strange because in that&nbsp;
personality I knew what we were doing. I knew that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:42.000 --> 01:40:47.440
my family was involved with these things. I knew&nbsp;
that this is what my family did for the federal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:47.440 --> 01:40:56.160
government. That that was our contribution as a&nbsp;
family to the CIA, to the Pentagon, to the feds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:56.160 --> 01:41:03.200
to the White House. that was our contribution is&nbsp;
we went in and we got rid of people and I could&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:03.200 --> 01:41:09.600
remember all that and that's just how it was. And&nbsp;
some in the family knew and some didn't. Some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:09.600 --> 01:41:16.800
my brothers and sisters have no idea. All of them&nbsp;
I would say in their conscious state of mind and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:16.800 --> 01:41:22.000
even in a subconscious state they wouldn't even&nbsp;
know because it would be hidden from them. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:22.000 --> 01:41:28.400
stuff's all compartmentalized even within the&nbsp;
families. But I was a part of that part of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:28.400 --> 01:41:35.600
family where we were used to get rid of people.&nbsp;
And so my uncle was there. He was talking to Cat&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:35.600 --> 01:41:40.960
on the comm system. Cat was up on the building&nbsp;
somewhere. We were deep in the city of Kobe in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:40.960 --> 01:41:47.200
a van in a dark alley. And my uncle got me&nbsp;
moving. He gave me more drugs to wake me up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:47.200 --> 01:41:53.440
Got me all hyped up again on drugs. We got me&nbsp;
into my operational suit. I was made to put on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:53.440 --> 01:41:59.600
this one piece suit with no markings. You're not&nbsp;
allowed to have any markings of any kind. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:59.600 --> 01:42:07.040
just a generic straight suit. It was a one piece&nbsp;
and that was it. I wasn't even allowed to wear&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:07.040 --> 01:42:15.840
my underpants, Emma, because they didn't want any&nbsp;
anything that could identify you as an individual.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:15.840 --> 01:42:22.720
So you were stripped of everything and put into&nbsp;
this uniform with no markings. They did give me&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:22.720 --> 01:42:29.360
nice boots and then um we were harnessed up&nbsp;
and my uncle he had these devices that were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:29.360 --> 01:42:36.240
made for suctioning cupping basically to glass&nbsp;
and we were next to a glass building. We were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:36.240 --> 01:42:44.720
parked in the alley by a big glass skyscraper&nbsp;
and we would attach to those suction cups which&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:44.720 --> 01:42:50.320
were electronically controlled. You didn't have to&nbsp;
sit there and pump it or anything like that. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:50.320 --> 01:42:58.080
put it on and it would attach to the glass. And&nbsp;
then you had a strap with a carabiner that you'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:58.080 --> 01:43:04.240
be able to stand in and you're attached to two of&nbsp;
these. You got two of them. And you'd attach one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:04.240 --> 01:43:09.440
You'd stand up. you'd attach another stand up and&nbsp;
you'd basically be able to walk up the building&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:09.440 --> 01:43:16.640
this way and I was attached to my uncle. My uncle&nbsp;
did the same thing and we were able to we did a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:16.640 --> 01:43:22.720
test first to make sure everything was working and&nbsp;
then up we went and we ascended this building and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:22.720 --> 01:43:28.800
it's a lengthy process. It's not super fast. So,&nbsp;
we go up this building and I can remember getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:28.800 --> 01:43:37.120
up there and we reached an area where it was a&nbsp;
divide between two buildings and we had to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:37.120 --> 01:43:42.400
across it. And this is where the pendulum jump&nbsp;
was set up that we had been practicing in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:42.400 --> 01:43:49.600
Boisee Valley. There was this big great big sign&nbsp;
up above on the wall of this giant building and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:49.600 --> 01:43:53.920
we were way above the city. I can remember&nbsp;
looking down and I wasn't afraid of heights&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:53.920 --> 01:44:01.280
in that personality at all. It was like, "Oh,&nbsp;
cool. We are way the hell up here and my uncle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:01.280 --> 01:44:08.400
he called into Cat. She was across on the&nbsp;
other building's uh top and he called into her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:08.400 --> 01:44:13.680
said we were over there. We'd reached that point&nbsp;
and then she came over to where we were." And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:13.680 --> 01:44:19.520
way it worked is you had an anchor point at each&nbsp;
end. So, we had an anchor point where we were and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:19.520 --> 01:44:25.760
she had an anchor point on her side and there&nbsp;
were ropes that were connected up above on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:25.760 --> 01:44:32.800
sign and they were tied off right there and you&nbsp;
would swing and come up and land at that anchor&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:32.800 --> 01:44:40.080
point and you'd set your anchor. Now you're here.&nbsp;
You could release yourself, jump and fall and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:40.080 --> 01:44:45.760
come back over to the other side and connect. Now&nbsp;
you're anchored on that side. It was a very quick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:45.760 --> 01:44:52.080
efficient way to move from point A to B. And so we&nbsp;
all did the jump and that was quite a jump. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:52.080 --> 01:44:58.320
was a huge jump. And we jumped through that and&nbsp;
we landed on the other side. And when I landed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:58.320 --> 01:45:05.120
Emma, we had trained for it. When we had trained&nbsp;
in Boyisey, I had landed wrong on one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:05.120 --> 01:45:11.040
landings and it had tweaked my back. And my uncle&nbsp;
